<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.postland-verify — the ASYNC post-land full-suite net. Every 5 min: is origin/main's
  TREE already stamped green? If yes it abstains in ~1s; else it runs the full check-set (bash -n +
  bats tests/) in a DISPOSABLE detached worktree and, on a reproducible red, bisects the culprit +
  pages. StartInterval (not calendar) closes the window "a red landed at 09:00 sits unseen until the
  04:00 nightly"; RunAtLoad false — a login must not kick off a full suite. PATH prepends
  ~/.claude/bin AND /opt/homebrew/bin (bats/shellcheck/jq) via bash -c so $HOME expands at runtime.
  C10: OPERATOR loads it. Kill switch: POSTLAND_VERIFY=off (or bootout).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.postland-verify</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"; if [ -x /usr/sbin/taskpolicy ]; then exec /usr/sbin/taskpolicy -c utility "$HOME/.claude/scripts/postland-verify.sh" --run-if-needed; fi; exec "$HOME/.claude/scripts/postland-verify.sh" --run-if-needed</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>10</integer>

    <!--
      NO ProcessType KEY, DELIBERATELY (2026-08-11, backlog 70dff02dcf4a).

      This job declared `ProcessType Background` until today. That key applies Darwin's darwinbg
      TASK ROLE, and the task role is a ONE-WAY FLOOR: every descendant is pinned at PRI 4
      (E-core confined) and NOTHING inside the job can lift it. Measured on this box:

          taskpolicy -c background   -> PRI 4, but a child's `-c utility` LIFTS it to PRI 20
          taskpolicy -b (= this key) -> PRI 4, and a child's `-c utility` still reads PRI 4
          taskpolicy -B -p <pid>     -> still PRI 4 (post-spawn un-set does not lift it either)

      That floor silently defeated the demotion machinery this repo already built. The corpus is
      launched as `nice -n 19 taskpolicy -c background bats …`, but `bats` PATH-resolves to
      ~/.claude/bin/cc-bats, whose default band is `utility` — so OUTSIDE this job the corpus
      really runs at PRI 20, and only under this key did it run at PRI 4. Two populations of the
      same corpus on the same box: scheduled (here, PRI 4) p50 3.11h vs session-invoked (PRI 20)
      p50 0.98h, against LAND_PIPELINE_V2 §8's 2h trigger. The plist was the whole band.

      Nice and LowPriorityIO stay: `nice` provably does not move PRI on Darwin (nice -n 19 alone
      still reads PRI 31) and LowPriorityIO is an I/O tier, not CPU confinement — so neither is
      the term that caused this, and both remain the polite default for the runner's own work.
      The corpus keeps its own demotion, which now takes effect: cc-bats clamps it to `utility`.

      THE REPLACEMENT IS `utility`, NOT "nothing". Dropping the key alone would leave the runner's
      own shell at PRI 31, and "we un-demoted the verifier" is a fair reading of that — direction C's
      risk in DEPLOY_GATE_CONVERGENCE.md §5. So ProgramArguments now execs through
      `taskpolicy -c utility`, which is the same band every other actuator in this repo moved to at
      2514226e: still below interactive, P-core eligible, and — unlike the task role — LIFTABLE, so
      cc-bats' own `-c utility` on the corpus is a no-op re-clamp rather than a fight. The verifier
      is demoted; it is simply no longer confined to the E-cores. Fail-open: no taskpolicy(8) ⇒ exec
      the runner directly rather than not run at all.

      Full derivation: docs/plans/LAND_PIPELINE_V2.md §8; invariant pinned by
      tests/postland-band-floor.bats — if a future macOS makes darwinbg liftable from inside,
      that suite goes red and this decision gets re-derived rather than inherited.
    -->

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/claude-postland-verify.stdout.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/claude-postland-verify.stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
